"type":"text","value":" runs the handler\nsynchronously up to its first "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await"},{"type":"text","value":", so a synchronous confirmation found no\npersisting request and applied at once. It acknowledged nothing. Registration\nthen installed the optimistic overlay over the confirmed row, and nothing\nretired it:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the row kept its optimistic value with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$hasPendingWrites: true"},{"type":"text","value":" after the\ntransaction completed;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the next remote write to the key reported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin: 'local'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The oracle missed it because its grammar wrote every source batch after the\nedit call returned. No generated history reached the handler's synchronous\nbody."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The gap was found while classifying survivors of a code-weight mutant run on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". A probe for mutant B4 showed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" violating the documented\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$hasPendingWrites"},{"type":"text","value":" contract in this history."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"repair-and-witnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repair and witnesses"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The grammar lets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"edit"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":" steps carry a source batch that the\nshared handler writes before it returns, about one step in four. The model\napplies that batch with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sync"},{"type":"text","value":" right after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"author"},{"type":"text","value":", and both views are\nallowed publication cuts. The driver asserts that the handler wrote the\nbatch."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Six pinned replays confirm an insert, an update, and a delete inside their\nown handlers, immediate and not, then settle and receive a later remote\nwrite."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sampling witness requires the fixed campaign (seed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"86103"},{"type":"text","value":") to generate\nin-handler batches for edits and deletes, immediate and not, with rows."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each direct path now registers the transaction, schedules its cleanup, and\nrecomputes optimistic state before it commits. The production change is net\n−2 lines."}]}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"34095aa6d"},{"type":"text","value":" (oracle only)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7 failed of 95: 5 of 6 pinned cases and both campaigns. The first failure is the batch publishing the server row as synced before the overlay."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3ab428439"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"95 passed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant: one path commits before it registers (insert, update, delete)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure: 4, 4, and 3 of 95"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant: one path registers, commits, then recomputes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure: 2 of 95 on each path"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The immediate delete case also passed before the repair: an immediate delete\nbatch applies at once either way, and the delete leaves no overlay to retire."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The handler writes one batch, synchronously, before any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await"},{"type":"text","value":". A batch\nwritten after an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await"},{"type":"text","value":" was already in the grammar as an ordinary sync\nstep."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transactions from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTransaction"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOptimisticAction"},{"type":"text","value":" register\nthrough "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutate()"},{"type":"text","value":" before the caller commits, so they never had this gap.\nThis change adds no witness for them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Local-only collections reach the repaired path: their wrapper confirms\nsynchronously when no user handler is given. Their rows never report\npending writes, so the old order had no visible effect there."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"verification","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3ab428439"},{"type":"text","value":", with the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db"},{"type":"text","value":" Vitest, typecheck off: 200 files, 7,857 tests.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsc --noEmit"},{"type":"text","value":": no errors."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist"},{"type":"text","value":" (290 tests) and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm test:minified-db"},{"type":"text","value":" pass."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package unit tests: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query-db-collection"},{"type":"text","value":" 558, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"electric-db-collection"},{"type":"text","value":" 629,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offline-transactions"},{"type":"text","value":" 73."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"note-added-2026-10-03","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note added 2026-10-03"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The settlement contract changed after this record. A transaction's optimistic\nstate now drops when its mutation function settles. A source batch written\ninside the handler is held and publishes with that drop, and it is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin: 'local'"},{"type":"text","value":" because it was committed while the transaction persisted.\nA write committed after settlement is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'remote'"},{"type":"text","value":". The evidence above is\nhistorical."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"source-batches-written-inside-a-mutation-handler","text":"Source batches written inside a mutation handler","level":1},{"id":"law","text":"Law","level":2},{"id":"gap","text":"Gap","level":2},{"id":"repair-and-witnesses","text":"Repair and witnesses","level":2},{"id":"limits","text":"Limits","level":2},{"id":"verification","text":"Verification","level":2},{"id":"note-added-2026-10-03","text":"Note added 2026-10-03","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Source batches written inside a mutation handler\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `34095aa6d` (oracle extension on `f2f92c5b2`).\nRepair executable revision: `3ab428439`.\n\n## Law\n\nA direct `insert`, `update`, or `delete` hands its request to the\nCollection's handler. The handler may confirm the request through sync before\nit returns. That source batch is the same event as a batch written while the\nnew request is active: it waits for settlement unless it is immediate or a\ntruncate, and ordinary publication then retires the accepted snapshot.\nAuthority: the optimistic-history contract in\n`packages/db/tests/optimistic-history-oracle.ts` (\"After success it remains\nas an accepted local snapshot until source acknowledgement retires it\") and\nthe virtual-property definitions in `docs/guides/live-queries.md`.\n\n## Gap\n\nThe direct paths in `packages/db/src/collection/mutations.ts` committed the\ntransaction before they registered it. `commit()` runs the handler\nsynchronously up to its first `await`, so a synchronous confirmation found no\npersisting request and applied at once. It acknowledged nothing. Registration\nthen installed the optimistic overlay over the confirmed row, and nothing\nretired it:\n\n- the row kept its optimistic value with `$hasPendingWrites: true` after the\n  transaction completed;\n- the next remote write to the key reported `$origin: 'local'`.\n\nThe oracle missed it because its grammar wrote every source batch after the\nedit call returned. No generated history reached the handler's synchronous\nbody.\n\nThe gap was found while classifying survivors of a code-weight mutant run on\n`state.ts`. A probe for mutant B4 showed `main` violating the documented\n`$hasPendingWrites` contract in this history.\n\n## Repair and witnesses\n\n- The grammar lets `edit` and `delete` steps carry a source batch that the\n  shared handler writes before it returns, about one step in four. The model\n  applies that batch with `sync` right after `author`, and both views are\n  allowed publication cuts. The driver asserts that the handler wrote the\n  batch.\n- Six pinned replays confirm an insert, an update, and a delete inside their\n  own handlers, immediate and not, then settle and receive a later remote\n  write.\n- A sampling witness requires the fixed campaign (seed `86103`) to generate\n  in-handler batches for edits and deletes, immediate and not, with rows.\n- Each direct path now registers the transaction, schedules its cleanup, and\n  recomputes optimistic state before it commits. The production change is net\n  −2 lines.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Owner on `34095aa6d` (oracle only) | 7 failed of 95: 5 of 6 pinned cases and both campaigns. The first failure is the batch publishing the server row as synced before the overlay. |\n| Owner on `3ab428439` | 95 passed |\n| Mutant: one path commits before it registers (insert, update, delete) | assertion failure: 4, 4, and 3 of 95 |\n| Mutant: one path registers, commits, then recomputes | assertion failure: 2 of 95 on each path |\n\nThe immediate delete case also passed before the repair: an immediate delete\nbatch applies at once either way, and the delete leaves no overlay to retire.\n\n## Limits\n\n- The handler writes one batch, synchronously, before any `await`. A batch\n  written after an `await` was already in the grammar as an ordinary sync\n  step.\n- Transactions from `createTransaction` and `createOptimisticAction` register\n  through `mutate()` before the caller commits, so they never had this gap.\n  This change adds no witness for them.\n- Local-only collections reach the repaired path: their wrapper confirms\n  synchronously when no user handler is given. Their rows never report\n  pending writes, so the old order had no visible effect there.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn `3ab428439`, with the built `dist`:\n\n- `packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 200 files, 7,857 tests.\n  `tsc --noEmit`: no errors.\n- `pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist` (290 tests) and\n  `pnpm test:minified-db` pass.\n- Package unit tests: `query-db-collection` 558, `electric-db-collection` 629,\n  `offline-transactions` 73.\n\n## Note added 2026-10-03\n\nThe settlement contract changed after this record. A transaction's optimistic\nstate now drops when its mutation function settles. A source batch written\ninside the handler is held and publishes with that drop, and it is\n`$origin: 'local'` because it was committed while the transaction persisted.\nA write committed after settlement is `'remote'`. The evidence above is\nhistorical.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Source batches written inside a mutation handler\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `34095aa6d` (oracle extension on `f2f92c5b2`).\nRepair executable revision: `3ab428439`.\n\n## Law\n\nA direct `insert`, `update`, or `delete` hands its request to the\nCollection's handler. The handler may confirm the request through sync before\nit returns. That source batch is the same event as a batch written while the\nnew request is active: it waits for settlement unless it is immediate or a\ntruncate, and ordinary publication then retires the accepted snapshot.\nAuthority: the optimistic-history contract in\n`packages/db/tests/optimistic-history-oracle.ts` (\"After success it remains\nas an accepted local snapshot until source acknowledgement retires it\") and\nthe virtual-property definitions in `docs/guides/live-queries.md`.\n\n## Gap\n\nThe direct paths in `packages/db/src/collection/mutations.ts` committed the\ntransaction before they registered it. `commit()` runs the handler\nsynchronously up to its first `await`, so a synchronous confirmation found no\npersisting request and applied at once. It acknowledged nothing. Registration\nthen installed the optimistic overlay over the confirmed row, and nothing\nretired it:\n\n- the row kept its optimistic value with `$hasPendingWrites: true` after the\n  transaction completed;\n- the next remote write to the key reported `$origin: 'local'`.\n\nThe oracle missed it because its grammar wrote every source batch after the\nedit call returned. No generated history reached the handler's synchronous\nbody.\n\nThe gap was found while classifying survivors of a code-weight mutant run on\n`state.ts`. A probe for mutant B4 showed `main` violating the documented\n`$hasPendingWrites` contract in this history.\n\n## Repair and witnesses\n\n- The grammar lets `edit` and `delete` steps carry a source batch that the\n  shared handler writes before it returns, about one step in four. The model\n  applies that batch with `sync` right after `author`, and both views are\n  allowed publication cuts. The driver asserts that the handler wrote the\n  batch.\n- Six pinned replays confirm an insert, an update, and a delete inside their\n  own handlers, immediate and not, then settle and receive a later remote\n  write.\n- A sampling witness requires the fixed campaign (seed `86103`) to generate\n  in-handler batches for edits and deletes, immediate and not, with rows.\n- Each direct path now registers the transaction, schedules its cleanup, and\n  recomputes optimistic state before it commits. The production change is net\n  −2 lines.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Owner on `34095aa6d` (oracle only) | 7 failed of 95: 5 of 6 pinned cases and both campaigns. The first failure is the batch publishing the server row as synced before the overlay. |\n| Owner on `3ab428439` | 95 passed |\n| Mutant: one path commits before it registers (insert, update, delete) | assertion failure: 4, 4, and 3 of 95 |\n| Mutant: one path registers, commits, then recomputes | assertion failure: 2 of 95 on each path |\n\nThe immediate delete case also passed before the repair: an immediate delete\nbatch applies at once either way, and the delete leaves no overlay to retire.\n\n## Limits\n\n- The handler writes one batch, synchronously, before any `await`. A batch\n  written after an `await` was already in the grammar as an ordinary sync\n  step.\n- Transactions from `createTransaction` and `createOptimisticAction` register\n  through `mutate()` before the caller commits, so they never had this gap.\n  This change adds no witness for them.\n- Local-only collections reach the repaired path: their wrapper confirms\n  synchronously when no user handler is given. Their rows never report\n  pending writes, so the old order had no visible effect there.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn `3ab428439`, with the built `dist`:\n\n- `packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 200 files, 7,857 tests.\n  `tsc --noEmit`: no errors.\n- `pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist` (290 tests) and\n  `pnpm test:minified-db` pass.\n- Package unit tests: `query-db-collection` 558, `electric-db-collection` 629,\n  `offline-transactions` 73.\n\n## Note added 2026-10-03\n\nThe settlement contract changed after this record. A transaction's optimistic\nstate now drops when its mutation function settles. A source batch written\ninside the handler is held and publishes with that drop, and it is\n`$origin: 'local'` because it was committed while the transaction persisted.\nA write committed after settlement is `'remote'`. The evidence above is\nhistorical.\n"}
